<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">The Bright Zone</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;Decades ago, a portal opened over the skies of Etheria, and two strange ships crashed on its surface. The renegade refugee First Ones who landed in the Scorpion Kingdom, and the Horde warlord who crashed in the kingdom of Brightmoon were welcomed with open arms . . . with mixed results. Now, the royal family has gone missing, and the Horde is leading a crackdown on all magic users in Brightmoon, remaking the land in his own despotic image.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adora of the Royalist Resistance and Princess Catra of Halfmoon gain a reputation for their daring raids against the invaders, one that only grows when Adora finds a strange sword, but on the other side of the conflict, a secret magic-user and the Horde's golden boy forge a bond of their own.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;TLDR; Catradora and Glimbow Roleswap AU&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>Cloudiana</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
      <dc:subject>
        <rdf:Bag>
          <rdf:li>Fanworks</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>General Audiences</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>She-Ra and the Princesses of Power (2018)</rdf:li>
